From 92496b1710398af23a466fae40b4abf6ae6bcdc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adbtrr_work6_sched_fixed <>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 19:27:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] apps/testcase: SMP placement diagnostic for the three
 residual failures

SCN-SMP-01, SCN-PRI-02 and SCN-AFF-04 remain red after PR 7465.  All three
reduce to one question: two unpinned tasks, two CPUs, and both tasks run on
CPU0 while CPU1 is not used.  AFF-04 states it outright, reporting
union_mask=0x1 against an expected 0x3, and it reports it only after its per
worker sample counts have passed, so the workers were running -- just never
on the second CPU.

Round-robin is not involved.  sched_select_cpu() decides where an unpinned
task is placed, and it can decline the second CPU for exactly three reasons:
the CPU is not in g_active_cpus_mask, the CPU is not idle and holds a task
the newcomer cannot displace, or it is idle and still not chosen.  The three
call for different fixes, so the cause has to be read rather than guessed.

Add TESTIOC_SCHED_CPUSTATE, which snapshots the placement state -- the head
of every g_assignedtasks[] list, the depth of each, the contents of
g_readytorun with each waiter's affinity mask, g_active_cpus_mask, and what
sched_select_cpu() returns for an unpinned task -- all inside one critical
section so that every field describes the same instant.

Add SCN-DIAG-01 through SCN-DIAG-04, which reproduce the idle system, the
AFF-04 pair, the PRI-02 ladder and a forced migration to the second CPU, and
print the snapshot underneath each.  The diagnostic reads scheduler state and
moves nothing; every scenario reports success so that a diagnostic run cannot
mask a regression elsewhere in the suite.
